[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
A fresh Kontrol-ID installation uses safe defaults and remains disabled until
it is enabled at Services > Kontrol-ID. Existing settings are preserved during
upgrades. The package manager installs the matching Kontrol Squid and
E2Guardian packages, including their transitive dependencies.

Kontrol-ID cannot coexist with pfSense-pkg-squid or the legacy
Kontrol-pkg-E2guardian5 GUI package because they own the same configuration
files. Remove the conflicting GUI package before installing Kontrol-ID. Do not
remove a shared squid, e2guardian or library package already required by the
matching Kontrol package.

The legacy domain-join Kontrol-ID pages are not used. Configure LDAP/Active
Directory under System > User Manager > Authentication Servers, select that
server under Services > Kontrol-ID, then generate an enrollment token on the
Stations tab and provision at least one Windows endpoint before enforcement.

Runtime databases in /var/db/kontrol-identity are intentionally preserved when
the package is removed. Squid and E2Guardian integration blocks are removed by
the package deinstall hook.
EOM
}
